
Background:
This series contains Diffuse Horizontal Irradiance for a location in Sinaloa, Mexico.
The Diffuse Horizontal Irradiance is the total amount of sun energy (in Watts per squared meter) arriving indirectly on a horizontal surface, ignoring the direct sunlight.

